// StartInboundRunWithBody Start a rule from outside
//
// The other half of the `INBOUND_WEBHOOK` trigger: an external system posts here and the rule's run begins, in the same engine every other trigger produces into.
// **This authenticates the rule, never a person.** There is no account behind the token and it grants nothing beyond starting that one rule - the run carries no actor, because naming one would invent an author for something nobody did. What the run may then do is its `run_as` account's business, checked per action exactly as it is for every other trigger.
