	// AcceptSuggestionWithBodyWithResponse Accept a suggestion
	//
	// Applies what was proposed, as the accepting person's own write: the ordinary use case, with the ordinary permission check, the ordinary validation and the ordinary history entry. A suggestion cannot grant anybody anything — somebody who could not make the change by hand cannot make it by accepting.
	// Two audit entries follow, deliberately: the acceptance and the write. "Who decided this" and "what changed" are two questions, and a year later only the first explains the second.
	// A suggestion made against an entry that has since been rewritten is **stale** and is refused (`409`, detail code `suggestions.stale`): applying it would attach a proposal about one state of the entry to a different one. Ask for a new suggestion instead.
	// The optional body carries what the person changed or added before accepting — an edited title, or the destination collection a jumble suggestion cannot know. It is merged over the proposal, and it is the caller's own input checked by the use case with the caller's own rights, exactly as if they had made the call themselves. The suggestion's target is never taken from either the proposal or the overrides: a proposal about one entry cannot be made to change another.
