// EnrollTotpWithBodyWithResponse Begin TOTP enrolment
//
// Mints the TOTP secret, sealed at rest through the envelope encryption every stored credential uses, and answers the provisioning URI and the ten recovery codes for the only time - the QR image is a client's job. The enrolment arms nothing yet: until a valid code confirms it, sign-in is unchanged, because an unconfirmed enrolment protects nobody and locks nobody out.
// Called with a bearer credential by a signed-in person, or with the pending credential a sign-in under tenant enforcement answered - the route an unenrolled administrator is routed into instead of into a session. Enrolling again before confirming replaces the unconfirmed secret; enrolling while armed is refused - disable first, with the password.
