// UpdateBackupScheduleWithBodyWithResponse Change a schedule, or switch it off
//
// Merge-patch: an absent key changes nothing. `enabled` is the field that matters most and the reason a `DELETE` is not the only answer - switching a schedule off keeps what somebody worked out about hours, zones and generations, and turning it back on costs one request rather than a form filled in again.
// Changing the rule, the zone or the switch recomputes when it is next owed, here rather than on every read. A rule with no occurrence inside a year stores no next moment and is not refused, for the reason creating one is not.
